---
/* Who runs this, and what the sites do with your data. Not an Impressum in
 * the German sense - a community project with no company behind it - but the
 * questions a company asks before it lets its people use a tool are answered
 * here, once, in plain words. It names no person and no place: the project
 * is many contributors, and the contact address is the project's. Linked
 * under the community row of the home page and from the foot of the sister
 * sites. */
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Page title="About abap2UI5" description="Who runs abap2UI5, what it is, and what the sites and the browser tools do with your data.">

<div class="wrap prose">
  <p class="crumb"><a href={base}>Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> About</p>
  <h1>About abap2UI5</h1>

  <h2>What it is</h2>
  <p>abap2UI5 is an open-source project: a framework for building UI5 apps in
  ABAP, released under the <a href="https://github.com/abap2UI5/abap2UI5/blob/main/LICENSE">MIT license</a>,
  and the sites around it - this page, the documentation, the samples, the
  playground and the browser tools, the addons. All of it is free, and none of
  it is a commercial offer. There is no company behind it, no product to buy
  and nothing to sign up for.</p>

  <h2>Who runs it</h2>
  <p>abap2UI5 is a community project, built and maintained by many
  contributors in their free time. The code and the sites live in the GitHub
  organisations <a href="https://github.com/abap2UI5">abap2UI5</a> and
  {" "}<a href="https://github.com/abap2UI5-addons">abap2UI5-addons</a>.
  To reach the maintainers, write to
  {" "}<a href="mailto:contact@abap2UI5.org">contact@abap2UI5.org</a> or open an
  issue in the repository the question is about.</p>

  <h2>Your data</h2>
  <p>The sites collect nothing. They are static pages served by
  {" "}<a href="https://pages.github.com/">GitHub Pages</a>: no accounts, no cookies
  of their own, no analytics, no tracking. Like any web server, GitHub may
  keep access logs; what it keeps and for how long is in
  {" "}<a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.</p>

  <p>The browser tools run in your browser. The Playground, the Layout Editor
  and the Report Converter compile and run your ABAP on your own machine; the
  code never leaves it unless you share a link yourself.</p>

  <p>The AI App Builder and the AI Agent talk to an AI model only when you
  enter your own API key. Then what you type, and the code the tool works on,
  is sent to the provider that key belongs to (OpenAI, Anthropic, or a server
  you name, including one on your own machine) under that provider's terms.
  The key is held in your browser for the visit and is never sent anywhere
  else. Without a key, nothing is sent at all.</p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>The framework and the tools are provided as they are, without warranty of
  any kind, as the MIT license says. Before you run anything on a system you
  care about, read the code - it is all there.</p>
</div>

</Page>
